@startuml
title Integrated Strategy and Observer - Roziyeva Yasmina's modules
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
class ArenaRun {
  + advance(dt, input)
  + cycleBehavior()
  + setLogEnabled(enabled)
  + close()
}
abstract class Enemy <<Strategy Context>> {
  - behavior: BehaviorStrategy
  + setBehavior(behavior)
}
interface BehaviorStrategy <<Strategy>> {
  + calculateMovement(enemy, worldView, dt): Vec2
  + desiredVelocity(enemy, worldView, dt): Vec2
  + name(): String
}
class PatrolBehavior <<Concrete Strategy>>
class ChaseBehavior <<Concrete Strategy>>
class FleeBehavior <<Concrete Strategy>>
class IdleBehavior
class AiSystem {
  + update(world, view, dt)
  + changeBehavior(world, enemyId, next, tick): boolean
}
class World <<Lifecycle Publisher>>
class ArenaRules <<Rule Publisher>>
class EventBus <<Subject>> {
  + subscribe(type, listener): Subscription
  + publish(event)
  + drainDeferred()
  + close()
}
interface "EventListener<E>" as Listener {
  + onEvent(event)
}
interface Subscription {
  + close()
}
class HudObserver <<Concrete Observer>> {
  + score(): int
  + health(): int
  + result(): Optional
  + close()
}
class EventLogObserver <<Concrete Observer>> {
  + lines(): List<String>
  + close()
}
ArenaRun *--> World
ArenaRun *--> ArenaRules
ArenaRun *--> AiSystem
ArenaRun *--> HudObserver
ArenaRun *--> EventLogObserver : optional
ArenaRun *--> EventBus
Enemy o--> BehaviorStrategy
AiSystem ..> Enemy : applies intent only
BehaviorStrategy <|.. PatrolBehavior
BehaviorStrategy <|.. ChaseBehavior
BehaviorStrategy <|.. FleeBehavior
BehaviorStrategy <|.. IdleBehavior
AiSystem --> EventBus : BehaviorChanged
World --> EventBus : lifecycle events
ArenaRules --> EventBus : rule events
EventBus o--> Listener : exact-class subscriptions
EventBus ..> Subscription
HudObserver --> Subscription : retains and closes 3 handles
EventLogObserver --> Subscription : retains and closes 6 handles
note bottom of EventBus
publish normally delivers synchronously.
Nested publications drain after the outer callback batch.
Observers register typed lambdas through EventListener.
end note
@enduml
